>>
Rule 1 (tensor input must be at least 2-D for fliplr)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 3 (tensor input dtype is unrestricted, but dimensionality must still be ≥ 2)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_1) ∧ ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 4 (tuple-of-tuples represents a valid 2-D array-like input with at least one row)
{v_1 : tuple(tuple(int ⊎ float ⊎ bool ⊎ str))} |= v_1.len ≥ 1
